  "summary": "Pakaja also known as Ibora Oke, or simply as Kaja is a type of Yoruba dress style worn by men and women in different styles.",
  "description": "Pakaja also known as Ibora Oke, or simply as Kaja is a type of Yoruba dress style worn by men and women in different styles. Pakaja is described as to pass a Yoruba Country Cloth from under the arm to the shoulder. It is a Toga like clothing style. Kaja is the name of the outfit itself while to Pa Kaja is the verbal act of wearing it which may also substitute as the name of the dressing style.\n\nPakaja can be donned in any fabric of choice.",
